{
 "slug": "budapest-water",
 "lines": [
  {
   "o": 0.481,
   "text": "70 million litres of hot water rise under Budapest every day. And you'd never guess what it's doing down there.",
   "chunks": [
    "*70 MILLION LITRES*",
    "OF *HOT WATER*|RISE UNDER *BUDAPEST*",
    "EVERY DAY.",
    "AND YOU'D NEVER GUESS",
    "WHAT IT'S DOING|*DOWN THERE.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 7.719,
   "text": "So where does all that hot water come from?",
   "chunks": [
    "SO WHERE DOES|ALL THAT HOT WATER",
    "*COME FROM?*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 10.148,
   "text": "Here, Earth's crust is thin. It heats up about one degree every 20 metres down.",
   "chunks": [
    "HERE, EARTH'S CRUST|IS *THIN.*",
    "IT HEATS UP ABOUT|*ONE DEGREE*",
    "EVERY *20 METRES* DOWN."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 16.176,
   "text": "Rain sinks deep into the Buda Hills, heats up, and rises back through a fault line.",
   "chunks": [
    "*RAIN* SINKS DEEP|INTO THE *BUDA HILLS,*",
    "HEATS UP,",
    "AND RISES BACK|THROUGH A *FAULT LINE.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 21.567,
   "text": "Result? 123 hot springs and wells. But that's not the strange part.",
   "chunks": [
    "RESULT?",
    "*123* HOT SPRINGS|AND WELLS.",
    "BUT THAT'S NOT|THE *STRANGE PART.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 26.681,
   "text": "The Romans built 14 baths here. The Ottomans added more, still open nearly 500 years later.",
   "chunks": [
    "THE *ROMANS* BUILT|*14* BATHS HERE.",
    "THE *OTTOMANS* ADDED MORE,",
    "STILL OPEN NEARLY|*500 YEARS* LATER."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 33.424,
   "text": "Some regulars look like they never got out.",
   "chunks": [
    "SOME REGULARS|LOOK LIKE THEY",
    "*NEVER GOT OUT.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 35.976,
   "text": "But the water wasn't just warming people. It was eating rock.",
   "chunks": [
    "BUT THE WATER WASN'T|JUST WARMING PEOPLE.",
    "IT WAS *EATING ROCK.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 39.852,
   "text": "Most caves are dug by rain from above. These were dug by hot water... from below.",
   "chunks": [
    "MOST CAVES ARE DUG|BY RAIN *FROM ABOVE.*",
    "THESE WERE DUG|BY HOT WATER...",
    "*FROM BELOW.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 45.51,
   "text": "So what's down there now?",
   "chunks": [
    "SO WHAT'S DOWN THERE|*NOW?*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 47.052,
   "text": "Behind a metal door near a busy road: a flooded cave, about six kilometres long.",
   "chunks": [
    "BEHIND A *METAL DOOR*|NEAR A BUSY ROAD:",
    "A *FLOODED CAVE,*",
    "ABOUT *SIX KILOMETRES* LONG."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 52.557,
   "text": "Divers swim through it, in warm water, under a hill full of houses.",
   "chunks": [
    "*DIVERS* SWIM THROUGH IT,",
    "IN WARM WATER,",
    "UNDER A HILL|*FULL OF HOUSES.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 57.062,
   "text": "No traffic down there. Best commute in Budapest.",
   "chunks": [
    "NO TRAFFIC|DOWN THERE.",
    "*BEST COMMUTE*|IN BUDAPEST."
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 60.224,
   "text": "Down there: fossil shark teeth. In Hungary, which has no sea... now.",
   "chunks": [
    "DOWN THERE:|*FOSSIL SHARK TEETH.*",
    "IN *HUNGARY,*|WHICH HAS NO SEA...",
    "*NOW.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 65.462,
   "text": "Budapest doesn't just have hot springs. It's sitting on one.",
   "chunks": [
    "BUDAPEST DOESN'T JUST|HAVE HOT SPRINGS.",
    "IT'S *SITTING ON ONE.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 69.348,
   "text": "And the twist? That cave is still growing.",
   "chunks": [
    "AND THE *TWIST?*",
    "THAT CAVE IS|*STILL GROWING.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 72.357,
   "text": "Right now, hot water is still dissolving the rock. Very... very... slowly.",
   "chunks": [
    "RIGHT NOW, HOT WATER|IS STILL *DISSOLVING*|THE ROCK.",
    "VERY...",
    "VERY...",
    "*SLOWLY.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "o": 78.205,
   "text": "This is Bhoogol. Follow for more Geography Fun Facts.",
   "chunks": [
    "THIS IS *BHUGOL.*",
    "FOLLOW FOR MORE|GEOGRAPHY FUN FACTS."
   ]
  }
 ],
